{"conversation_id":"db2bad0c-45ac-4457-810e-d23de99ca337","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I'll start by reading [1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase2-signoff.prompt.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792962000000-architect-datomic-q-phase2-signoff.prompt.md) and the architectural rules in [datom.world.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/datom.world.md) to understand the Phase 2 signoff requirements and design constraints.\nLet's check the architect and orchestrator role definitions in [architect.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/agents/roles/architect.md) and [orchestrator.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md), as well as the existing Phase 2 review findings and Phase 4b sign-off precedent in `collab/`.\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-26 13:03:33 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-26 20:03:33 +07\nCoding-Agent: agy\nSession-ID: db2bad0c-45ac-4457-810e-d23de99ca337\n\n# Lead System Architect Sign-Off Review — `dao.space.query.datomic` Phase 2 (`216e8efbe`)\n\n**Reviewed Range**: `master...datomic-q-p2-ci` (`a9dd014e2..216e8efbe`, 10 files changed, `+686/-80`; disjoint from `a9dd014e2..master` at `f5397a150`).\n**Firsthand Verification**:\n- **JVM (`clojure -M:test` in `.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes`)**: `dao.space.query-aggregates-test` + `dao.space.datomic-query-conformance-test` + `dao.space.query.datomic-test` — **61 tests, 342 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors** (BLAKE3 digest `17b53dd3edcc6d9c2760ce2cec49166fa1abe7d900b4465bb468aaaa813dc6cb`, 101 cases verified live); `dao.space.query.execution-test` + `dao.space.query.datomic-execution-test` — **64 tests, 451 assertions, 0 failures**.\n- **Jolt J2 Manifest Gate (`src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` on `master` against `.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test`)**: **FAILS** with `UNLISTED dao.space.query-aggregates-test` (see **Question 4, M1**). Jolt value/math probes (`build/tools/jolt`) confirm `dao.space.query-aggregates-test` is portable on Jolt once listed.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Frozen Aggregate Conventions, IEEE-754 Scope, and Numeric-Carrier Host Split\n\n**Conforms to [`dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L334-L351) and [`datomic-q-v1.errata.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L168-L216) (E15).**\n\n- **Single evaluation kernel, zero adapter semantics**: All six deterministic aggregates (`distinct`, `median`, `variance`, `stddev`, `(min n ?x)`, `(max n ?x)`) are owned by [`aggregate-fns`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2237-L2260) and [`parse-aggregate`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2263-L2285) in `dao.space.query`. The adapter (`dao.space.query.datomic`) only mirrors structural admission in [`aggregate-arities`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L335-L347) and [`check-find`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L411-L434), keeping `rand` and `sample` explicitly excluded (`:unsupported`, no entropy ownership).\n- **Deterministic cross-host ordering and deduplication**:\n  - [`distinct`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2257) delegates to `content-distinct`, matching `count-distinct` (`cbor/content-key`), with the documented host-set collapse (`1.0M` / `1.00M` on JVM/Jolt; `+0.0` / `-0.0` on JVM/Dart).\n  - [`numeric-order`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2181-L2193) defines a strict total order modulo `cbor/content=` (`cbor/num-compare` first, then `preferred-tie`: exact numeric before `float64`, else shorter canonical CBOR encoding), making `median`, `variance`, `stddev`, `(min n ?x)`, and `(max n ?x)` invariant to group arrival order across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt.\n- **IEEE-754 determinism scope**: [`agg-variance`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2222-L2234) (population `÷ n`, `0.0` for `n = 1`), `stddev` ([`sqrt-double`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2200-L2204)), and even-count [`agg-median`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2207-L2219) fold doubles in `numeric-order` using only IEEE-754 basic operations (`+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `sqrt`), which are correctly rounded on every target host. Scoping bit-identical cross-host expectations to exact-double-representable integer inputs (without introducing an epsilon tolerance) directly honors [`dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L345-L347).\n- **Carrier host-split accuracy**: Verified against [`dao/host/number.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc):\n  - `cbor/float64` wraps in a `Float64` carrier **only** on ClojureScript (`Double` on JVM/Jolt, `double` on ClojureDart — all native `number?`).\n  - `cbor/decimal` wraps in a `Decimal` carrier on ClojureScript and ClojureDart (`BigDecimal` is `number?` on JVM/Jolt).\n  - [`host-double`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2168-L2178) refuses non-`number?` carriers loudly in arithmetic paths (`variance`, `stddev`, even-count `median`), while pure order statistics (odd-count `median`, `(min n ?x)`, `(max n ?x)`) preserve carriers on every host. Corpus cases (`agg.median-tied-kinds` on `clj`/`cljd`, `agg.median-tied-kinds-carrier-refused` on `cljs`, `agg.median-tied-kinds-odd` on all hosts, `agg.variance-carrier-refused` on `cljs`/`cljd`) cover every host cell without silent skips.\n- *Minor Phase 3/5 documentation note*: Because `(max n ?x)` takes `(take n (reverse (sorted-numeric xs)))` ([`query.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2252)), on a numeric tie `{1, 1.0}` `(max 1 ?v)` returns `[1.0]` (reversing `numeric-order`, pinned in [`query_aggregates_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc#L185)), whereas 1-arg `(max ?v)` uses `portable-max` (`preferred-tie`) and returns `1`. Self-consistent for slicing one total order from opposite ends; worth a 1-sentence note in E15 before Phase 5 oracle differential runs.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Static E3 and E13 Refusals, Error Taxonomy, and Conservative Boundary\n\n**Conforms to [`dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L649-L735) and E3 / E13 in [`datomic-q-v1.errata.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L33-L143).**\n\n- **E3 (`:find` / `:with` / aggregate / `pull` boundness)**:\n  - [`check-find-vars-bound!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2405-L2421) runs in `:parse` inside [`q-with-state`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2532) before input realization or `:where` evaluation. Core throws `ex-info` with `{:var v}` only; [`classify-core-failure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L576-L580) maps it to `:invalid-request` (`:cognitect.anomalies/incorrect`) with empty context `{}` (zero leaked bindings, `::dbs`, or source handles).\n  - [`clause-bound-vars`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2387-L2402) excludes `not`/`not-join`, restricts `or-join` to its join vector, unions `or` branches, and strips `(first clause)` of predicate/fn clauses `[(f ?x) ?y]`. Thus `[:find ?x :where [(\u003c ?x 10)]]` is rejected statically (`?x` only inside `(first clause)`), while an unbound fn input not named in `:find` (`[:find ?y :where [(+ ?x 1) ?y]]`) passes static check and is rejected at runtime (`\"Unbound variable in fn clause\"`). E3's conservative-boundary note ([`datomic-q-v1.errata.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L43-L45)) is honest and sufficient until Phase 3 adds rule-invocation / `or`-branch consistency checks.\n- **E13 (non-tuple relation refusal)**:\n  - [`realize-base-st`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L651-L653) immediately refuses eager non-tuple `:dao.space.query/relation` slots (`5`, `{:a 1}`) via [`tuple-source?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L502-L506) / [`refuse-relation`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L509-L512) (`{:reason :invalid-relation}`), while leaving `delay?` slots unforced at realization/planning (preserving the lazy covered-index `:rows` invariant) and refusing non-tuple delayed values when forced in [`force-relation`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L515-L523).\n  - Unbounded adapter calls classify `{:reason :invalid-relation}` as `:invalid-request` with empty `{}` context; bounded adapter calls continue to fail closed earlier at [`source-step`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L613-L614) (`:unsupported` / `:bounded-source-unqualified`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Honesty and Soundness of the `numeric-value` Comparison Rule\n\n- **Honest by design (not a hidden tolerance)**: On ClojureScript, decoding `{\"float64-bits\": ...}` from [`datomic-q-v1.json`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.json) produces a `dao.host.number/Float64` carrier, whereas core arithmetic (`avg`, `median`, `variance`, `stddev`) produces a raw JS `number` (and JS cannot distinguish integral doubles like `41.0` or `7.0` from integers `41` or `7`). Scoping `\"numeric-value\"` per-case in [`datomic-q-v1.README.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.README.md#L70-L74) and comparing leaf numerics via `(zero? (cbor/num-compare a b))` in [`cell-same?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc#L321) tests **exact mathematical equality** with **zero epsilon**, while strict kind preservation on JVM is independently pinned with `cbor/content=` in [`query_aggregates_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc).\n- **Missed harness defect (M2 — non-blocking, deferrable to Phase 3)**: In [`cell-same?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc#L322-L324), set equality is implemented as:\n  ```clojure\n  (and (= (count a) (count b))\n       (every? (fn [x] (some #(cell-same? x %) b)) a))\n  ```\n  Because `cell-same?` is non-injective across numeric kinds (`(cell-same? 1 1.0) =\u003e true`), one-way `every?` plus equal cardinality is **not a bijection** when a set contains kind-distinct, value-equal tuples: `(cell-same? #{[1] [1.0]} #{[1] [999]})` evaluates to **`true`**. I verified all 17 `\"numeric-value\"` cases in [`datomic-q-v1.json`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.json): none has value-tied elements in the same expected set, so all 101 current cases are genuinely verified. Hardening `cell-same?` (bidirectional coverage or equivalence-class frequency comparison) touches only [`datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc#L322-L324) (zero corpus/digest churn) and can ride in Phase 3.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Architectural \u0026 Gate Defects Missed by the Review Chain\n\n1. **[BLOCKING MERGE CONDITION — Gate Defect M1] `dao.space.query-aggregates-test` is unlisted in [`src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L265-L270)**:\n   - Branch `datomic-q-p2-ci` adds [`test/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/dao/space/query_aggregates_test.cljc). On `master`, [`check-manifest!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L324-L340) scans `test/dao/space/**` before running any J2 lane mode.\n   - Running `check-manifest!` against `.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test` fails immediately:\n     `J2 manifest FAILED: UNLISTED dao.space.query-aggregates-test`.\n   - Merging `datomic-q-p2-ci` without adding `\"dao.space.query-aggregates-test\"` to `included` in [`src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj#L269-L270) would cause the fifth recurrence of the datomic-track unlisted-namespace break on `master` (and [`dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L924-L925) explicitly requires applicable pure query suites in the `jolt` lane).\n   - Firsthand Jolt probes verify every host operation used by `query_aggregates_test.cljc` (`Math/sqrt`, `BigDecimal` `number?`/`double`/set deduplication `[1.0M 1.00M]`, and `(number? (cbor/float64 1)) =\u003e true`). Add `\"dao.space.query-aggregates-test\"` to `included` in the merge commit (or single pre-merge commit) and execute its Jolt single-namespace run after `bb build:jolt-native`.\n2. **[Non-blocking P2/P3 — Defect M2] Asymmetric `set?` comparison in [`cell-same?`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc#L322-L324)**: Documented in Question 3; deferrable to Phase 3.\n3. **Disposition of GLM's two P3 findings \u0026 Phase 4b doc polish**:\n   - **GLM P3 #1 ([`datomic-q-v1.errata.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/test/resources/dao/space/datomic-q-v1.errata.md#L202))**: Not actually stale — `datomic-q-v1.errata.md` documents the core `dao.space.query/q` harness (per E11), and core [`parse-aggregate`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc#L2271) still throws `\"Unknown aggregate in :find\"` (pinned by `agg.rand-excluded`), whereas the adapter throws `:unsupported` `\"randomized aggregates are excluded from the profile\"` ([`datomic.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/src/cljc/dao/space/query/datomic.cljc#L424)). Mentioning both layers in E15 is optional Phase 3 polish.\n   - **GLM P3 #2 (pre-existing non-var aggregate arg validation, e.g. `(count [1 2])`)**: Pre-existing (`check-declared-symbols` already blocks bare symbols); safely deferred to Phase 3 syntax tightening.\n   - **Phase 4b doc carries ([`dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L626-L633) and [`L801-L809`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/datomic-p2-fixes/docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md#L801-L809))**: Verified accurate and complete.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Sign-Off Verdict\n\nSIGNED OFF WITH CONDITIONS: Add `\"dao.space.query-aggregates-test\"` to `included` in `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj` at merge time (and verify that namespace under the Jolt runner once `bb build:jolt-native` is built on `master`) so `check-manifest!` and the J2 lane stay green; carry `cell-same?` set-bijection hardening (`test/dao/space/datomic_query_conformance_test.cljc:322-324`), the 1-line `(max n ?x)` tie-order note in E15, and the two Phase 3 syntax/errata P3s into Phase 3.\n","duration_seconds":1125.139709,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":309896,"output_tokens":43285,"thinking_tokens":29077,"cache_read_tokens":5860367,"total_tokens":353181}}
